> There might have been a discussion to be had about this new validation being either "throw" or "set a default value" depending on the type. I'm not sure that it feels right.

For the validation behavior here, I'm trying my best to match the behavior of how inspector assignment translates to GDScript, which is based on the following results from the testing script:

```yaml
// GDScript
_stringValueNotNull: 
_stringNameValueNotNull: 
_nodePathValueNotNull: 
_nodeValueNotNull: <null>
_resourceValueNotNull: <null>
_dictionaryValueNotNull: {  }
_arrayValueNotNull: []
_intValueNotNull: []
_stringArrayValueNotNull: []

//C#
_stringValueNotNull: Null
_stringNameValueNotNull: Null
_nodePathValueNotNull: Null
_nodeValueNotNull: Null
_resourceValueNotNull: Null
_dictionaryValueNotNull: Null
_arrayValueNotNull: Null
_intValueNotNull: Null
_stringArrayValueNotNull: Null
```

- `String`, `StringName`, and `NodePath` defaults to an empty instance if left unassigned in GDScript (where in C# they default to `Null`), so they are initialized with an empty value in this pr.
- `Node`, and `Resource` reference defaults to `Null` if unassigned, so they are null checked in this pr.
- `Dictionary[,]` and `Array[]` defaults to an empty collection (where in C# they default to `Null` unless you click and expand them inside the inspector), I took the liberty to null-check them as they are possible to be set to null from the inspector, but I'm also ok with initialize them as well.
- `Packed(\w+)Array` defaults to empty array, so they are initialized to `Array.Empty<$1>` if left unassigned.

Here is a brief summary:

|Godot Type|Defaults in GDScript|Defaults in C#|Behavior in this PR when unassigned|
|----|--------------------|---------------|-------------------|
|`String`|Empty String|`null`|Initialized to `string.Empty`|
|`StringName`|Empty StringName|`null`|Initialized to `new StringName()`|
|`NodePath`|Empty NodePath|`null`|Initialized to `new NodePath()`|
|`Node`|`null`|`null`|`ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull`|
|`Resource`|`null`|`null`|`ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull`|
|`Godot.Collections.Dictionary[,]`|Empty Dictionary|`null`|`ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull` or initialized to `new Dictionary<TKey,TValue>()`|
|`Godot.Collections.Array[]`|Empty Array|`null`|`ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull` or initialized to `new Array<T>()`|
|`Packed(\w+)Array`|Empty PackedByteArray|`null`|Initialized to `Array.Empty<$1>()`|

